    <td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
        <tr>
          <td><span class="postbody">You guys were over level 40 and bitching about the 40+ exp grind.  I was early 30's I think and soloing (haha) and grouping with Geradith a bit if I remember correctly.
<br />

<br />
Horizons is a pass for me.  There's a huge emphasis on tradeskilling and quite honestly, the client-side lag and poor graphic performance was worse than EQ's.  If I can get lag, poor performance and tradeskills, I might as well stick with EQ that I've already spent almost FIVE years on.  No reason to start something new that's similar.
<br />

<br />
EQ2?  Yeah it's a logical progression.  Personally, if the EQ graphic engine revamp happens (rumor) it'll stick me in there for a lot longer.  It should make the game run better.
<br />

<br />
My only concern is World of Warcraft.  It's the only game that I'm worried will strip me from EQ completely.  WC is one of my all time favorites and it's shaping up to be a nice mix of EQ/LDoN and WC lore.  I can't wait for the beta..<br />_________________<br />- Me</span><span class="gensmall"><i></i></span></td>
